  "prompt": "Which expression is equivalent to $\\frac{(12x^{8}y^{5})}{(3x^{3}y^{9})}$?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$4x^{5}y^{4}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{(4x^{11})}{(y^{14})}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{(4x^{11})}{(y^{4})}$",
    "D": "$\\frac{(4x^{5})}{(y^{4})}$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "D",
  "explanation": "First, simplify the coefficient: $\\frac{12}{3}=4$. Then apply the quotient rule for exponents: $\\frac{x^8}{x^3}=x^{8-3}=x^5$ and $\\frac{y^5}{y^9}=y^{5-9}=y^{-4}$. Finally, convert the negative exponent: $y^{-4}=\\frac{1}{y^4}$, giving $\\frac{4x^5}{y^4}$.",
